From: OpenMandriva
Subject: [PATCH] Bug 2054387 - Qt: handle late devicePixelRatio / HiDPI scale

On Wayland, QScreen/QWindow often report devicePixelRatio()==1 at startup
and only update after the surface is configured. ScreenHelperQt only
refreshed on screen add/remove, and nsWindow never notified Gecko of scale
changes (GTK has OnScaleEvent → BackingScaleFactorChanged).

Result: intermittent half-size, blurry fonts/content that looks fine only
when DPR was ready before first layout. good.png (DPR 2) vs bad.png (stuck
at 1): same browser chrome size, ~2x smaller web content / fuzzy text.

- Listen for QScreen geometry/DPI signals; RequestRefreshScreens() API
- Handle QEvent::DevicePixelRatioChange; re-check on expose/move/resize
- Refresh ScreenManager + PresShell::BackingScaleFactorChanged on change

diff -u -N -r /tmp/ff-0014-regen-old/widget/qt/QtWindowBridge.cpp /tmp/ff-0014-regen-new/widget/qt/QtWindowBridge.cpp
--- a/widget/qt/QtWindowBridge.cpp
+++ b/widget/qt/QtWindowBridge.cpp
@@ -190,6 +190,12 @@
                                     int(windowState()));
       return handled;
     }
+    case QEvent::DevicePixelRatioChange:
+      // Qt 6: fired when Wayland/X11 buffer scale for this window changes.
+      // Without this, Gecko keeps the startup scale (often 1.0) and pages
+      // render half-size and blurry on HiDPI.
+      mWidget->OnScalePossiblyChanged();
+      return QWindow::event(aEvent);
     default:
       break;
   }
